            <ArticleTitle>Some common causes of hip pain. Physical diagnosis is the key.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>189-92, 194-5, 198</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A variety of disorders can cause pain about the hip. The significance of these various disorders varies. Obviously, appropriate treatment cannot be initiated until a correct diagnosis is made. The classic methods of physical diagnosis must be used. X-ray studies or bone scans are most often only confirmatory but frequently necessary.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
